{"/api/discogs/artist/105944/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"105944","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:105944","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":9507,"name":"Franco & Grimm"},{"id":90787,"name":"Upgrade Two Point Two"},{"id":103333,"name":"Foam People"},{"id":118488,"name":"Baloo"},{"id":418041,"name":"Mayham Franco"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":510508,"name":"Marcel Franke"},{"active":true,"id":626009,"name":"Sander Grimmelius"}],"namevariations":["Upgrade One"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/105944-Upgrade-One-Point-Two","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/109392/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"109392","image":"https://i.discogs.com/R-FdbAnbX2Xp3wqAv10mKPnngVd6sVg9RWS-s4SLSsI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:399/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwOTM5/Mi0xNjI2NzkwNzU1/LTk0ODYuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/bm9eA0wodNQznC62AOlUC8SGLKdZhaQB5Hb2_L_CEAY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwOTM5/Mi0xNjI2NzkwNzU1/LTk0ODYuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"French Hip Hop crew from Marseille, formed in 1989. \nBy the early 90’s a number of rap stars such as NTM and MC Solaar had emerged from the Paris suburbs and started making their mark upon the French music scene. Meanwhile the multi-cultural town of Marseille, in the South of France, was proving to be fertile ground for a second wave of the rap movement, spearheaded by the group IAM (pronounced as English \"I am\").\n\nIn the beginning the group was born in 1984/85 when rapper [a=Akhenaton] and [a=DJ Khéops] performed under the name of \"Lively Crew\". In 1988 the group's name was changed to \"B Boys Stance\".\nOne year later [a=Shurik'n], producer [a=Imhotep], dancer [a=Kephren] and [a=Freeman (3)], a dancer who started to rap, joined them. The name of the group was changed again - and so in 1989 IAM (Imperial Asiatic Men) was born.\n\nThey autoproduced a cassette named \"Concept\" that swiftly spread their name and their fame in the whole town. This tape became kind of mythic and within a short time every youth had heard the name of \"IAM\".\n\nIn the following years IAM produced five very successful albums. For 2013 the upcoming album \"I AM Legend\" is planned in collaboration with [a=Ennio Morricone].\n\n[a=Freeman (3)] officially left the group in 2009.\nSince a long time [a=Said] is always seen together with the group. He performs with them on stage and in the studio and sometimes he is mentioned to be the sixth member of them.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:109392","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":699740,"name":"Pascal Perez"},{"active":true,"id":789936,"name":"Eric Mazel"},{"active":true,"id":880803,"name":"Geoffroy Mussard"},{"active":true,"id":1190642,"name":"Philippe Fragione"},{"active":true,"id":1646141,"name":"Malek Brahimi"},{"active":true,"id":1908255,"name":"François Mendy"}],"namevariations":["I AM","I Am","I'am","I.A.M.","Jam","jam","アイ・アム"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/109392-IAM","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/iamlegroupe","http://genius.com/artists/Iam","http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0406268","http://www.instagram.com/iam.officiel","http://twitter.com/iam","","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IAM_(band)","http://www.youtube.com/channel/UC6ixw3qmStEkmftFYB9HP3w","http://www.youtube.com/user/IamVEVO"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/12425083/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"12425083","image":"https://i.discogs.com/tdt_r9YhNE5zYghcFKQ0fAjmkfwuDEQXaEH_AXy0PwM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:400/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEyNDI1/MDgzLTE2ODQyNzY1/NDYtMzcxNS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/-byZUjG8QM98keEDLvpdpa2dKJ1g8GoBSr46bVPUDc4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEyNDI1/MDgzLTE2ODQyNzY1/NDYtMzcxNS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Fliss Mayo & Zebb Dempster are Dual Monitor, or ‘The UK Genre Alchemists’ as they are called by those in the know. The pair have found great success in bolting together myriad different rhythms from the worlds of bass, techno and sound system culture with everything from dembow to dub and jungle. Dual Monitor are based in Liverpool and Bristol. They have released on labels much as CloudCore, ec2a, Nerve Collect and N-Face. ","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:12425083","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/12425083-Dual-Monitor","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/dualmonitor","https://www.instagram.com/_dualmonitor_/","https://dualmonitor.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1415/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1415","image":"https://i.discogs.com/eqJIeVZlfh25qNqpkNBFksfmUwl9M6DAQMKxKpUJJpI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:335/w:250/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0MTUt/MDAxLmpwZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/GMrMQlu40JiAnu6z8r2OyHHTvTddZ-nUfQ9ha2h_aAw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0MTUt/MDAxLmpwZw.jpeg","profile":"Producer from Barnsley, South Yorkshire. Latterly moved to Hertford.\r\n\r\nRob Haigh's first release as Omni Trio was on his own [l=Candidate Records] label in early 1993. This caught the ear of Hertford based trio [a=2 Bad Mice] who helped sign Haigh to [l=Moving Shadow]. Through the nineties Haigh developed a unique style of what has become known as ambient (or 'intelligent') Drum and Bass and released six acclaimed albums. The Omni Trio sound is notable for its intricate orchestrated production and atmospheric sound palette. ","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1415","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":22944,"name":"London Steppers"},{"id":25456,"name":"Silent Storm"},{"id":74421,"name":"Robert Haigh"},{"id":90992,"name":"Sema"},{"id":152380,"name":"Splice (2)"},{"id":196086,"name":"Haute Control"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Omnitrio","The Omni Trio"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1415-Omni-Trio","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.myspace.com/c1943","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omni_Trio","https://omnitrio.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/152709/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"152709","image":"https://i.discogs.com/P7pegOu3mlDKbVkKrgEFiY3Cfd-ruaHhkkdgDv_2WyQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:450/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1Mjcw/OS0xMzk1Nzc1NDQ1/LTIxODkuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/C6tjkKF_5PB-TxNL0ww6h50ec1FP8xcyVSTFY5A1pLs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1Mjcw/OS0xMzk1Nzc1NDQ1/LTIxODkuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Hip Hop / Drum & Bass MC from Brooklyn,NY, United States\r\nT.R.A.C. has been very involving in many different scenes in his music career. Struck by the bug at a very young age, music has always been one of the most influential things in his life. As an MC he knows how to rock a crowd, as a lyricist he can surely put words together in a fashion, but its the art of making music where T.R.A.C. excels. Not wanting to be seen as just a rapper, he wants to be respected as a vocalist/musician and MC.\r\nThrough out his musical journey, the New York native has touched on many different genres with Hip Hop effort. On his first '2000 feature with DJ ICUE “Next Level $hit” became an underground classic on Liquid Sky Records. The fusion of the 2 styles was seen as provocative at the time. Nonetheless, The experience of this had set the stage of what was to come in the future.\r\nAs a Konkrete Jungle resident and NYC scene supporter, T.R.A.C. has been seen performing with top tier Dj's and artist abroad. From NYC junglist Dj's like Odi, Dara, Soul Slinger, and LionDub to name a few, to overseas heavies like Jumpin Jack Frost, Dego (4hero), The Upbeats, Skream and within recent times was seen rocking the mic for the re-known Roni Size and the legendary DJ LTJ Bukem.\r\nBack on the Hip Hop side of things, TRAC does what he considers “classic style Hip Hop. In love with mostly sampled sounds, he has teamed with the likes of UK legend Lewis Parker on a couple of occasions. From 2007's Boosey n Hawks entitled “Lewis Parkers' Home Grown Hip Hop” to Lp's more recent releases such as Dangerous Adventures.\r\nIn 2009, a friend handed him a copy of an album called Visioneers. A compilation of very well orchestrated covers that were done by UK (4hero) Legend Marc Mac. Being inspired from the album , T.R.A.C. went and searched for him via the internet. After a couple of conversations a new relationship was made firing the BK MC into new grounds. The tandem are 3 projects deep with music including his well received 2011 Omniverse/BBE debut album “The Network”. Marcs amazing soundscapes topped with T.R.A.C.'s vocals have been reviewed by critics on blogsites and magazines as “addictive” and “refreshing” to Hip Hop, garnishing 6stars in a Euro magazine(Oct OE4).\r\nWith a couple of feature spots to come in the future along with another upcoming over-viewed EP in the works his catalog keeps growing with quality music. Expect to hear and see more of this talented MC throughout the year. His goal remains the same. To Rule And Conquer.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:152709","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":5380823,"name":"Terrence Nicholas"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["T.R.A.C","TRAC","Trac"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/152709-TRAC","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/t-r-a-c","https://www.facebook.com/tracmuzik","https://twitter.com/trac_","http://youtube.com/teenickz","https://trac-mc.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2334338/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2334338","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2334338","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1917837,"name":"Civilian Flexibility"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2334338-Time-Travel","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3118855/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3118855","image":"https://i.discogs.com/hjy-5kyGQSiYLxSK1rv56YmLadu5E3b96DltmUat1Yw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxMTg4/NTUtMTYzMzk3NzMw/Mi02NzM3LnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/m15aA1gkRwY-NJnA2jIzFmxWpMFhY-FWwah-EEPBSWo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxMTg4/NTUtMTYzMzk3NzMw/Mi02NzM3LnBuZw.jpeg","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3118855","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3118855-Feloneezy","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3136632/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3136632","image":"https://i.discogs.com/C3yhTx77VYbgxpXLThv2NYVu534lXwKZa-k2GGsX3I8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:387/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxMzY2/MzItMTQxMjIxOTQ2/Ni0yMDA0LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/H-pA0vHnRxelsgUgElLddPgKNOx9YmebIjVYI0THyNM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxMzY2/MzItMTQxMjIxOTQ2/Ni0yMDA0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Canadian musician, singer, songwriter.\r\nFormed in 2013.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3136632","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":2632182,"name":"Sans AIDS"},{"id":2869874,"name":"Peter Sagar"},{"id":17571972,"name":"ps goner"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3136632-Homeshake","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/homeshake","http://homeshake.bandcamp.com/","http://www.sinderlyn.com/#!homeshake/fasj5"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3354069/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":